  "result": "I opened the issue: https://github.com/acme/textstats/issues/13 (\"word_count returns 1 for empty string instead of 0\"). I didn't change any code.\n\n- **Where:** `word_count` is in `textstats/__init__.py`, line 6.\n- **Likely cause:** it returns `len(text.split(\" \"))`, and `\"\".split(\" \")` gives `['']`, so the count is 1.\n- **Related problem:** splitting on a single space also miscounts input with repeated, leading or trailing spaces. `average_word_length` in the same file uses `text.split()`, which avoids this. The issue mentions it.\n- **Issue contents:** it has steps to reproduce (`word_count(\"\")`), expected 0 versus actual 1, and the location and cause. The agent also added acceptance criteria asking for a test of the empty-string case in `tests/test_textstats.py`. You didn't ask for those, so edit them out if you don't want them.",
